„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ»It shall be for the priests that are sanctified of the sons of Zadok; which have kept my charge, which went not astray when the children of Israel went astray, as the Levites went astray.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙpAnd this oblation of the land that is offered shall be unto them a thing most holy by the border of the Levites.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter0«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÒAnd over against the border of the priests the Levites shall have five and twenty thousand in length, and ten thousand in breadth: all the length shall be five and twenty thousand, and the breadth ten thousand.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙxAnd they shall not sell of it, neither exchange, nor alienate the firstfruits of the land: for it is holy unto the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter0«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙĞAnd the five thousand, that are left in the breadth over against the five and twenty thousand, shall be a profane place for the city, for dwelling, and for suburbs: and the city shall be in the midst thereof.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙñAnd these shall be the measures thereof; the north side four thousand and five hundred, and the south side four thousand and five hundred, and on the east side four thousand and five hundred, and the west side four thousand and five hundred.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÎAnd the suburbs of the city shall be toward the north two hundred and fifty, and toward the south two hundred and fifty, and toward the east two hundred and fifty, and toward the west two hundred and fifty.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚAnd the residue in length over against the oblation of the holy portion shall be ten thousand eastward, and ten thousand westward: and it shall be over against the oblation of the holy portion; and the increase thereof shall be for food unto them that serve the city.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙLAnd they that serve the city shall serve it out of all the tribes of Israel.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAll the oblation shall be five and twenty thousand by five and twenty thousand: ye shall offer the holy oblation foursquare, with the possession of the city.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter0«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚ®And the residue shall be for the prince, on the one side and on the other of the holy oblation, and of the possession of the city, over against the five and twenty thousand of the oblation toward the east border, and westward over against the five and twenty thousand toward the west border, over against the portions for the prince: and it shall be the holy oblation; and the sanctuary of the house shall be in the midst thereof.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÔMoreover from the possession of the Levites, and from the possession of the city, being in the midst of that which is the prince's, between the border of Judah and the border of Benjamin, shall be for the prince.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter0«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses—„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙdAs for the rest of the tribes, from the east side unto the west side, Benjamin shall have a portion.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙbAnd by the border of Benjamin, from the east side unto the west side, Simeon shall have a portion.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙWAnd by the border of Simeon, from the east side unto the west side, Issachar a portion.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙXAnd by the border of Issachar, from the east side unto the west side, Zebulun a portion.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙSAnd by the border of Zebulun, from the east side unto the west side, Gad a portion.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¦And by the border of Gad, at the south side southward, the border shall be even from Tamar unto the waters of strife in Kadesh, and to the river toward the great sea.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŠThis is the land which ye shall divide by lot unto the tribes of Israel for inheritance, and these are their portions, saith the Lord GOD.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter0«first_verseªlast_verse"¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙdAnd these are the goings out of the city on the north side, four thousand and five hundred measures.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ›And the gates of the city shall be after the names of the tribes of Israel: three gates northward; one gate of Reuben, one gate of Judah, one gate of Levi.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ„And at the east side four thousand and five hundred: and three gates; and one gate of Joseph, one gate of Benjamin, one gate of Dan.¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd at the south side four thousand and five hundred measures: and three gates; one gate of Simeon, one gate of Issachar, one gate of Zebulun.¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‚At the west side four thousand and five hundred, with their three gates; one gate of Gad, one gate of Asher, one gate of Naphtali.¦layout ªlast_verse"…¤book§chapter0«first_verse#ªlast_verse#¦verses‘„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙrIt was round about eighteen thousand measures: and the name of the city from that day shall be, The LORD is there.¦layout ªlast_verse#